/E (Increased inflation: The Irish grocery retail market is experiencing significant pressure as consumers face increased cost-of-living concerns, rising costs and an increasing need for value. The Competition and Consumer Protection Commission CCPC 2025 have stated that grocery prices in Ireland have increased by 27% since 2021, with non-alcoholic beverage and food prices rising a further 4.6 percent between June 2024 and June 2025 \(CCPC, 2025\). This consistent inflation places significant pressure on households and has increased demand for transparency and accurate pricing information. The Irish Times 2025 also reports grocery inflation reaching 6.5 percent, consistently outpacing general inflation \(Pope, 2025\). These economic trends strongly support the need for a real-time price comparison app like PriceBeo. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
