776 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 231 0 R
/E (The financial model is based on a scalable digital platform, where growth is driven primarily by increasing monthly active users and improving conversion rates over time. As the user base expands, revenue increases across premium subscriptions, advertising, and affiliate income streams, while costs grow at a slower rate.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
777 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 231 0 R
/E (Operating expenditure is structured across marketing, product development, and administrative costs. Marketing represents the primary driver of early growth, supporting user acquisition and brand awareness. Staffing costs are based on a lean structure in Year 1, with gradual increases in salaries and headcount, including the addition of a developer and customer support role as the business scales.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
778 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 231 0 R
/E (Technology-related costs include ongoing app development, cloud infrastructure, and external development support, with a transition to in-house development by Year 3. Costs are largely variable and linked to platform usage, including server, API, and payment processing fees.)
/Pg 41 0 R
